AtomicFit: Compiled Source Materialfor SRS
Team: Alexander Marchiano, Jonathan Gouw, Luiesrelio (Luwi)
This document merges all AtomicFit related material (problem background, interviews,
personas, ideation, value proposition, core features, flow, MVP breakdown, and the low
fidelity wireframes) into one place. It is organized so each section can feed a matching
SRS section.
1. Product Overview
Product name: AtomicFit (team name: The Gym Bros)
Origin problem (Alex's problem): People who exercise alone must pay attention to their
exercise program, form, running distance, and repetitions, and also remember to record all
of it. Tiredness and shortness of breath make them forget to log, so workout records
become inaccurate, progress slows, and motivation drops. A personal trainer solves this
by tracking progress and correcting form, but most people cannot easily access one.
Guiding question: Wouldn't it be nice if everyone had easy access to a personal trainer
that tracks their exercise, adjusts their workouts, and plans accordingly?
Redefined problem statement (Persona 2.0 version): Can we give people affordable, low
effort access to expert level guidance that automatically tracks their progress, adapts
their program to real life disruptions, and designs a plan suited to their individual needs
without requiring the time, money, or specialized knowledge a personal trainer normally
demands?
Redefined problem statement (SRE version): Can we have easy access to a personal
trainer who can reduce the cognitive load of exercise, track progress automatically, and
accurately design our fitness program according to our own specific needs?
Core insight: The pain is not forgetting numbers. The pain is that a lost count makes the
session feel like it "didn't count." Demotivation hits hardest for people whose only reward
is visible progress.
Two root causes the product targets:
1. In-workout friction (typing, losing count, losing position mid-set).
2. Post-lapse guilt (broken streaks, "it didn't count" mindset, restarting after a break).
