6. Feature Inventory (from the Flow deck)
Core flow:
1. Check In: no judgment diagnostic question after a long break; gives users control over
expectations.
2. Calibration: prevents DOMS; triggers Smart Ease-In to prevent injuries.
3. Instant Stop / Validation Net: Micro-Session Auto Classifier logs short sessions as
"power blasts" and adds completed reps to the weekly volume bucket.
Fundamental features:
Manual logging of exercises, sets, reps, and weight.
Activity recording for cardio (distance, pace, elevation).
Charts and graphs (strength gains, volume trends, body weight changes).
Exercise database with demonstration videos or animations for correct form.
Adaptive programming that adjusts future workouts based on logged performance and
recovery.
Core unique features:
Auto-Ramp-Down: reduces target weight after a long break.
No-Judgment Diagnostic Quiz: quick energy question to create a short workout based
on condition.
Micro-Session Auto-Classifier: adjusts goals when a workout is cut short so it can still
be marked successful.
Extra features:
Voice Quick Log ("3 sets of 10 squats").
Lock Screen Quick Add (add reps or sets without unlocking).
"Save Point" Resume Card (e.g. "Set 3, stopped at rep 6", continue with one tap).
Weekly Rep and Distance Bucket.
Asynchronous Set Stitching (combines sets completed at different times into one
workout).
